WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.990
<b>Big News</b>

3
00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:18.000
<b>Pangaea Castle
Mary Geoise</b>

4
00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:15.340
The World Conference known as

5
00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:17.630
the Reverie has concluded.

6
00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:20.720
It is a meeting that
occurs every four years,

7
00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:23.310
where a council of 50
world leaders gather,

8
00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:26.600
representing some of
the 170 nations

9
00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:29.980
affiliated under
the World Government.

10
00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:37.280
As it often does,
the event ended with

11
00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:39.360
a great sense of uncertainty.

12
00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:43.240
The representatives went home
without much reassurance.

13
00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:48.330
Then. One week later.

14
00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:53.340
Goodness,
that's always such a trek.

15
00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:53.200
<b>Ryugu Palace, Ryugu Kingdom
Fishman Island</b>

16
00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:55.000
It's good to be home.

17
00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:58.550
Heading up to the surface world
always takes so much out of me.

18
00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:02.550
Uh, I wanted to thank you
for escorting us back safely!

19
00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:04.470
Mister Luffy's Grandpa!

20
00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:07.600
I bet that excursion must have
been pretty draining on you!

21
00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:09.560
Soundin' tuckered
there out, Neptune!

22
00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:13.640
You can say that again!

23
00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:15.630
Garp, why don't you
take a load off

24
00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:15.730
and get some
well-deserved rest, okay?

25
00:01:15.730 --> 00:01:17.610
and get some well-deserved rest?

26
00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:21.030
Well, maybe I'll stay for
a cup of tea or two,

27
00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:22.700
but not much longer.

28
00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:25.720
Wouldn't want to be lax
at a time like this.

29
00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:26.070
The Reverie always
seems to result in chaos.

30
00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:30.370
The Reverie always seems
to result in chaos.

31
00:01:30.370 --> 00:01:31.790
To put it simply, when you have

32
00:01:31.790 --> 00:01:34.500
50 heads of state
in the same room,

33
00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:36.840
you can't expect them
to get along.

34
00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:39.840
Each country is only thinking
about their own problems.

35
00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:42.300
The major powers will
stare each other down

36
00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:46.260
and let the smaller nations
squabble over this and that.

37
00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:51.080
If you've got the
resources and technology,

38
00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:54.910
you're the shot caller.

39
00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:57.250
They say all countries
are equal,

40
00:01:57.250 --> 00:02:00.250
but those words
never hold any weight.

41
00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:01.350
As long as there are wealth
and religious differences,

42
00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:05.190
there will never be true
equality, unfortunately.

43
00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:13.970
When it's time to shake,
they grin,

44
00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:16.520
then stomp each other's
feet under the table.

45
00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:18.440
These rulers can
speak for themselves,

46
00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:20.560
but can they speak
for all their citizens

47
00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:23.110
or the citizens of
other nations?

48
00:02:23.110 --> 00:02:25.740
The "round table"
is nothing but a myth.

49
00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:26.860
Quite true.

50
00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:28.450
As they say,
you could cut the tension

51
00:02:28.450 --> 00:02:30.320
in that room with a knife.

52
00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:32.330
The source of that
friction is a history

53
00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:34.370
that runs deep indeed.

54
00:02:34.370 --> 00:02:37.200
And we are no exception.

55
00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:39.370
Alas, the issues
of the past are not

56
00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:43.750
swept away so easily,
or quietly.

57
00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:43.840
The way I see it,
as long as no blood's spilled

58
00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:46.010
The way I see it,
as long as no blood's

59
00:02:46.010 --> 00:02:46.300
spilled at the end of the day,

60
00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:47.380
at the end of the day,

61
00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:49.600
then I'm willing
to call it peace.

62
00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:53.310
This year's Reverie
was bad though.

63
00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:55.480
Maybe I should have
said something sooner,

64
00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:57.940
but there was an
incident that happened.

65
00:02:57.940 --> 00:02:59.900
I haven't told anyone yet.

66
00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:03.490
It took place right after
the Reverie was dismissed.

67
00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:06.820
I got a report when I was
leaving on the ship.

68
00:03:06.820 --> 00:03:08.950
Let me preface this
by saying the Navy

69
00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:08.990
is using everything it's
got to settle this mess.

70
00:03:08.990 --> 00:03:12.200
is using everything it's got
to settle this mess.

71
00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:12.240
Don't fear humans
or the surface either!

72
00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:16.450
Don't fear humans,
or the surface either!

73
00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:17.830
What could've happened?

74
00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:19.910
The report must have
been rather serious

75
00:03:19.910 --> 00:03:22.670
for you to act this way, Garp.

76
00:03:22.670 --> 00:03:25.960
It concerns
the Alabasta Kingdom.

77
00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:30.920
Please say it isn't so.
Princess Vivi!

78
00:03:32.470 --> 00:03:35.760
Shortly after
the Reverie was dismissed,

79
00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:38.140
the reporters were abuzz
at the headquarters

80
00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:40.350
of the World Economic Journal.

81
00:03:40.350 --> 00:03:43.400
How are all these
things happening at once?

82
00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:46.230
It's one thing
after another! Jeez!

83
00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:49.000
We need
a catchy headline for this!

84
00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:53.210
Which one is
going on the front page?

85
00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:59.840
<b>Editor-in-Chief Morgans
World Economic Newspaper</b>

86
00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:57.330
Hey! This is big for us!

87
00:03:57.330 --> 00:03:59.910
Nothin' rakes in cash
like an obituary!

88
00:03:59.910 --> 00:04:01.120
That's the cover story, then!

89
00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:02.460
Patience!

90
00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:05.130
The resolution they
passed is juicy, too.

91
00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:06.880
And there was an
attempted murder.

92
00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:08.260
So I have a plan!

93
00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:09.630
What, Boss?

94
00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:11.760
For the first time ever,
we're running dual covers,

95
00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:13.590
a story on front and back!

96
00:04:13.590 --> 00:04:15.140
Okay!

97
00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:18.060
Sir! You've got a
telegram from the Government.

98
00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:20.730
Hm? This a check?

99
00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:23.020
Wow! Look at those zeros!

100
00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:24.190
So they want me to cover up

101
00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:26.940
one of these hot stories,
do they? Gah.

102
00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:28.980
Well, let's see which one it is.

103
00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:35.160
I ain't passing on
the biggest scoop of my life!

104
00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:36.010
There's no stopping this story!

105
00:04:36.010 --> 00:04:39.970
They can keep their damn money.

106
00:04:39.970 --> 00:04:41.220
You hear me?

107
00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:44.850
This is a big mistake.

108
00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:49.350
You're going to do as your told.
Is that clear?

109
00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:52.270
It's Cipher Pol?
Why are you here?

110
00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:53.690
To make sure that
you obey orders

111
00:04:53.690 --> 00:04:56.240
from the World
Government. Freeze!

112
00:05:00.950 --> 00:05:03.280
Don't mess with
"Big News" Morgans,

113
00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:07.450
if y'know what's good for you!

114
00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:11.880
When did this louse get in here?

115
00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:16.840
You know he's
a Government official, right?

116
00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:20.630
It's time to boogie. Now!

117
00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:23.010
We're compromised!

118
00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:28.480
I may be
a money-hungry scrooge,

119
00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:31.940
but above all,
I'm a journalist first!

120
00:05:31.940 --> 00:05:34.980
I get people's hearts dancing
with the stories I compose!

121
00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:36.610
I'm a DJ of the press!

122
00:05:36.610 --> 00:05:39.530
I decide what news
is fit to print!

123
00:05:43.660 --> 00:05:44.870
Mr. Morgans!

124
00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:48.080
King Wapol of
Drum Kingdom is calling!

125
00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:49.750
He is?

126
00:05:51.460 --> 00:05:53.250
What does he want?

127
00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:56.380
It sounds like
he has some leaked information!

128
00:05:56.380 --> 00:05:59.550
What?!

129
00:06:08.390 --> 00:06:09.770
What the heck?

130
00:06:09.770 --> 00:06:11.310
A special report?

131
00:06:19.230 --> 00:06:22.240
Don't cry. It'll be okay.

132
00:06:23.450 --> 00:06:25.660
Hm?

133
00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:30.620
Including the incident

134
00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:33.210
that the Government failed
to keep under wraps,

135
00:06:33.210 --> 00:06:36.000
the news report also
spread word of the decision

136
00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:38.250
the leaders reached
while at the Reverie.

137
00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:43.380
The disturbing news leaves
many in shock across the world.

138
00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:47.820
Impossible!
This news can't be true!

139
00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:57.060
<b>Revolutionary Army Headquarters
Kamabakka Kingdom</b>

140
00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:51.390
Don't buy into this poppycock,

141
00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:54.850
the WEJ's either making
this up or taking bribes!

142
00:06:54.850 --> 00:06:57.980
That bird is lying through
his smug little beak!

143
00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:02.860
I just know it!

144
00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:04.780
We're talking about Sabo!

145
00:07:04.780 --> 00:07:06.360
He's gotta be okay!

146
00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:08.740
He's not dead! There's no way!

147
00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:11.740
Take a deep breath. Stay calm.

148
00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:13.750
We need to confirm the facts.

149
00:07:13.750 --> 00:07:16.880
We've lost contact with
their entire team, though.

150
00:07:16.880 --> 00:07:19.170
Can we verify any of this?

151
00:07:19.170 --> 00:07:22.340
No. Please Sabo.

152
00:07:22.340 --> 00:07:24.630
You can't die.

153
00:07:25.130 --> 00:07:27.800
<b>Royal Escort Ship
The Kingdom of Goa</b>

154
00:07:26.590 --> 00:07:27.970
Whoa! Is she okay?

155
00:07:27.970 --> 00:07:30.430
What was he doing in Mariejois?

156
00:07:30.430 --> 00:07:32.930
That's my brother, for sure!

157
00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:40.400
<b>Foosha Village
The Kingdom of Goa</b>

158
00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:37.230
What's with Makino?

159
00:07:37.230 --> 00:07:39.270
I don't know,
she closed the bar today.

160
00:07:39.270 --> 00:07:40.730
Why?

161
00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:43.610
There's so much chaos
in the world right now.

162
00:07:43.610 --> 00:07:45.900
I could really use a drink.

163
00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:52.790
Sabo...

164
00:07:52.790 --> 00:07:56.920
We only just found out
that he was still alive, too.

165
00:07:52.830 --> 00:07:59.040
<b>Mt. Colubo
The Kingdom of Goa</b>

166
00:07:56.920 --> 00:08:03.630
How could this happen
to you? Sabo!

167
00:08:06.760 --> 00:08:09.680
<b>The Undersea Prison Impel Down</b>

168
00:08:09.330 --> 00:08:12.680
The world
sure can be a funny place!

169
00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:15.130
There's never a boring day!

170
00:08:15.130 --> 00:08:18.050
And we're just getting
to the good part now!

171
00:08:25.070 --> 00:08:27.280
<b>Hachinosu
The Pirate Island</b>

172
00:08:25.240 --> 00:08:29.610
Wakey, wakey!
Time to pack your bags!

173
00:08:29.610 --> 00:08:31.870
If the Navy wants
to get involved,

174
00:08:31.870 --> 00:08:34.790
I'll just take it myself!

175
00:08:39.670 --> 00:08:42.420
Jumping ahead to the present.

176
00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:50.930
<b>The Outskirts 
of Ebisu Town

Wano</b>

177
00:08:53.450 --> 00:08:54.490
Cu-lick.

178
00:08:57.720 --> 00:08:59.480
Coby? It's me.

179
00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:04.940
<b>Present Day
A Stretch of Open Sea</b>

180
00:09:03.690 --> 00:09:07.320
Hold on just a sec.
I need to find a better spot.

181
00:09:07.320 --> 00:09:09.610
Sure.

182
00:09:11.180 --> 00:09:13.490
Ah! That's right!
The "Sea"!

183
00:09:13.490 --> 00:09:13.550
The "Fog."

184
00:09:13.550 --> 00:09:16.430
The "Fog." Hmph.

185
00:09:16.430 --> 00:09:16.500
You're as diligent
as ever, I see.

186
00:09:16.500 --> 00:09:18.790
You're as
diligent as ever, I see.

187
00:09:18.790 --> 00:09:18.850
Well, I'm only following
the protocol is all, you know?

188
00:09:18.850 --> 00:09:22.500
Well, I'm only following
the protocol is all! You know!

189
00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:24.960
Oh, yeah! By the way!

190
00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:25.020
I have an urgent report
for you. Captain!

191
00:09:25.020 --> 00:09:28.770
I have an urgent report
for you, Captain.

192
00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:33.130
<b>X Drake
Navy Headquarters
Officer of SWORD, a Top Secret Special Force</b>

193
00:09:37.090 --> 00:09:38.550
You're serious?

194
00:09:38.550 --> 00:09:40.930
That's the current state
of affairs out there?

195
00:09:40.930 --> 00:09:42.180
Sadly.

196
00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:44.060
We're having trouble
keeping up with it all.

197
00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:47.270
<b>Captain Koby
Navy Headquarters
Member of SWORD</b>

198
00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:47.440
Even with every active
Marine on our side.

199
00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:49.860
For your situation,
it's going as planned,

200
00:09:49.860 --> 00:09:52.360
so the military won't
be getting involved.

201
00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:54.740
Not like we have
the manpower, anyway.

202
00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:56.240
Probably for the best.

203
00:09:56.240 --> 00:09:59.410
Wano and the World Government
aren't allied, regardless.

204
00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:03.620
So, tell me what you know about
Big Mom arriving at Onigashima.

205
00:10:04.780 --> 00:10:07.040
Gladly. The Navy's banking
on Kaido and Big Mom's

206
00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:09.830
long-standing grudge
to get explosive.

207
00:10:09.830 --> 00:10:12.210
We're hoping those two
take each other out.

208
00:10:12.210 --> 00:10:13.420
I thought so.

209
00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:15.460
Hate to report
this next bit then.

210
00:10:15.460 --> 00:10:17.130
I highly doubt
we can count on them

211
00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:20.260
being at each other's
throats anymore.

212
00:10:20.260 --> 00:10:23.510
It turns out they're teaming up.

213
00:10:24.670 --> 00:10:25.430
Huh? Wh-Wh-What?

214
00:10:25.430 --> 00:10:27.770
Are you joking with me?

215
00:10:31.820 --> 00:10:35.570
As for Straw Hat Luffy,
it's a stalemate.

216
00:10:35.570 --> 00:10:37.950
There's been no news
of his breakout.

217
00:10:37.950 --> 00:10:39.110
I should also mention,

218
00:10:39.110 --> 00:10:40.910
while I was in the
capital the other day,

219
00:10:40.910 --> 00:10:44.040
I happened to spot
Cipher Pol 0.

220
00:10:44.040 --> 00:10:47.250
Huh? Why are they in Wano?

221
00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:49.460
Really hoping I'm
wrong about this.

222
00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:51.420
But it would imply that
the Government's colluding

223
00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:56.130
with a pirate-ruled country
to conduct some nasty business.

224
00:10:58.380 --> 00:11:00.680
I'm sure you're
in a state of shock.

225
00:11:00.680 --> 00:11:03.340
I was too when I found out.

226
00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:16.400
In any case, where are you now?

227
00:11:16.400 --> 00:11:18.030
Traveling.

228
00:11:18.030 --> 00:11:20.740
I'm on my way to
the Island of Women.

229
00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:28.410
We're going to
capture Boa Hancock.

230
00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:30.500
What the hell?

231
00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:33.880
Why is there an entire fleet
crossing the Calm Belt?

232
00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:36.300
Wait, is that the Navy?

233
00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:38.800
Huh? Margaret!

234
00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:41.800
Whatever they want
with us, it can't be good.

235
00:11:43.590 --> 00:11:46.510
The news continued
to spread across the world.

236
00:11:47.930 --> 00:11:50.640
'Bout time! They shoulda
done this a long time ago!

237
00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:53.900
I know! It was wrong to
work with pirates anyway!

238
00:11:53.900 --> 00:11:55.440
Let 'em all die!

239
00:11:55.440 --> 00:11:58.440
There were many
who celebrated the report.

240
00:11:59.600 --> 00:12:01.820
Those dumb Government lapdogs

241
00:12:01.820 --> 00:12:03.450
are finally goin' away!

242
00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:04.660
Screw you, Empress!

243
00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:05.870
Screw you, Hawk-Eye!

244
00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:07.200
Screw you, Clown!

245
00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:11.410
You good-for-nothing looters
can just piss off!

246
00:12:11.410 --> 00:12:12.920
Those who had suffered

247
00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:15.500
at the hands of pirates
especially welcomed the news.

248
00:12:15.500 --> 00:12:18.960
Really? I'm no fan, but imagine
how the war in Marineford

249
00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:20.420
would've gone without them!

250
00:12:20.420 --> 00:12:22.760
The nobles voted on this?

251
00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:24.390
I bet the Navy acts right away.

252
00:12:24.390 --> 00:12:26.550
Are you absolutely
certain about this?

